# Onboard parameters for Vehicle 1
#
# STAGE 3a - HEIGHT REFERENCE ONLY. Independent of vision, UART and the container.
#
# This is the runaway-climb fix and it works on the vehicle as it stands today.
# Nothing here depends on external vision, so it is safe to apply before the
# UART link is repaired.
#
# Current state (May 7 dump):  EKF2_HGT_REF = 2 (Range), EKF2_BARO_CTRL = 0 (off),
# GPS off. Whenever the rangefinder stops delivering (above its range -- the VL53L1X
# driver maximum is 4 m -- over an obstacle, a rejected sample) there is then NO
# height aiding at all - the altitude estimate free-runs, the controller reads it
# as sinking, and commands a climb that never terminates. (Corrected 2026-10-15:
# EKF2_RNG_A_HMAX only applies in conditional mode, EKF2_RNG_CTRL = 1.)
#
# The essential fix is EKF2_BARO_CTRL = 1. This file also makes baro the
# reference; for range-as-reference indoors (PX4 v1.16 "Indoor (flat terrain)":
# HGT_REF 2, RNG_CTRL 2, BARO_CTRL 1) see fleet/SN0001-fixes-2026-10-15.params.
# Which one becomes the fleet default depends on the venue floor (flat or not).
#
# After loading: reboot the FC, then hover-test in position hold and confirm the
# altitude holds. Props off first; watch /fmu/out/vehicle_local_position z.
#
# Vehicle-Id	Component-Id	Name	Value	Type
1	1	EKF2_HGT_REF	0	6
1	1	EKF2_BARO_CTRL	1	6
